SUMMARY:[Knowledge Representation & Reasoning][Explainability & Interpretab
 ility] KR 2027 - Main-track abstract registration deadline (estimated)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Conference on Principles of Kno
 wledge Representation and Reasoning\nWebsite: https://kr.org/\nSource URL
 : https://kr.org/KR2026/call_main_track.html\nLocation: Buenos Aires\, Ar
 gentina\nTopics: Knowledge Representation & Reasoning\, Explainability & 
 Interpretability\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based / formal and symb
 olic AI\nConfidence: estimated\nLast checked date: 2026-10-07\nNotes: KR 
 Inc. announces Buenos Aires for its 2027 edition\, but no exact meeting o
 r submission dates were found. July meeting dates and February submission
  deadlines are annual proxies from KR 2026\, not organizer announcements.
  The 2026 ML and Explanation track informs the scope profile but is not a
 ssumed to be a confirmed 2027 track. M is an editorial estimate.\nScope: 
 Formal and symbolic AI centered on representing knowledge and drawing jus
 tified conclusions: knowledge bases\, description and non-classical logic
 s\, ontologies\, non-monotonic reasoning\, argumentation\, belief revisio
 n\, and reasoning about actions. Learning\, uncertainty\, and explanation
 s matter when grounded in knowledge representation or reasoning. The last
  published CFP includes a KR Meets Machine Learning and Explanation track
 \; this is not a general-purpose ML conference or a confirmed promise of 
 that 2027 track.\nAdditional topics: Machine Learning\, Probabilistic\, C
 ausal & Uncertainty ML\, Planning & Search\nScope sources (2026): https:/
 /kr.org/KR2026/call_main_track.html\, https://kr.org/KR2026/\nScope last 
 checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://kr.org/KR2026/call_main_track.html
END:VEVENT
